<title>GERMANY: German sugarbeet sowings delayed by cold weather.</title>
<headline>German sugarbeet sowings delayed by cold weather.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cold weather has pushed back German sugarbeet planting schedules after farmers made a start in some warm regions last week, a source at the national meteorological office DWD said.</p>
<p>&quot;The latest cold front with rain and even some snow has blocked everything...we need warmer temperatures in the first half of April and soils need to dry,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Low temperatures and some night frosts were forecast for the next six days when field work will be restricted because of the Easter holidays.</p>
<p>Last week, farmers on the Lower Rhine and Franconia started plantings but the bulk of the crop in Lower Saxony and Bavaria will not be sown before mid-April.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
